add_public_site_url_and_seo_head_compone.s:
Root gap: `src/app.html` (full file, already read) has no `<title>`, no meta description, no canonical/OG/Twitter tags — and `<svelte:head>` is used NOWHERE in `src/routes` (confirmed by a full-tree grep, zero matches). Every route — home, `/login`, every `/app/*` page — currently ships whatever `<title>` the browser defaults to (the bare URL) and no description at all. This is the foundational gap every other step in this plan builds on top of.

**1. A stable absolute base URL.** Canonical links, OG `url`/`image`, JSON-LD, the sitemap, and the RSS feed all need an absolute origin, and this repo has no custom domain configured yet (`wrangler.jsonc` has no `routes`/domain block — deploys only to `*.workers.dev`, confirmed). Rather than hardcoding a domain that will need to change the day a real domain is attached, add it as a plain (non-secret) var, read via this repo's existing `$env/dynamic/private` convention for ALL env access (per this repo's own CLAUDE.md rule — non-secret `[vars]` are read the same way as secrets, never via a different mechanism). Add to `wrangler.jsonc`'s existing `vars` block (line 90, currently `"vars": { "WS_ORIGIN": "wss://x2-ws.apexlinks.workers.dev" }`):
```jsonc
	"vars": {
		"WS_ORIGIN": "wss://x2-ws.apexlinks.workers.dev",
		"PUBLIC_SITE_URL": "https://x2.apexlinks.workers.dev"
	},
```
(confirm the actual deployed `*.workers.dev` URL matches this guess — derived from this same file's `"name": "x2"` plus the account subdomain implied by `WS_ORIGIN`'s `apexlinks.workers.dev` — before finalizing; update to the real value if `wrangler deployments list` or the Cloudflare dashboard shows something different. The moment a real custom domain is attached, this is the one line that changes — nothing else in this plan hardcodes a domain.) Add `PUBLIC_SITE_URL: SecretVal;` to the `QEnv` type in `src/lib/server/qdrant.ts` (already read, lines 57-65) so every server function's existing `env: QEnv` parameter can read it without a new type.

**2. A reusable head component.** Create `src/lib/components/SeoHead.svelte` (new file):
```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	let {
		title,
		description,
		path,
		image,
		noindex = false,
		jsonld
	}: {
		title: string;
		description: string;
		path: string;
		image?: string;
		noindex?: boolean;
		jsonld?: Record<string, unknown> | Record<string, unknown>[];
	} = $props();

	const SITE = 'x2';
</script>

<svelte:head>
	<title>{title} · {SITE}</title>
	<meta name="description" content={description} />
	<link rel="canonical" href="{path}" />
	{#if noindex}
		<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
	{:else}
		<meta name="robots" content="index, follow" />
	{/if}
	<meta property="og:type" content="website" />
	<meta property="og:site_name" content={SITE} />
	<meta property="og:title" content={title} />
	<meta property="og:description" content={description} />
	<meta property="og:url" content={path} />
	{#if image}<meta property="og:image" content={image} />{/if}
	<meta name="twitter:card" content={image ? 'summary_large_image' : 'summary'} />
	<meta name="twitter:title" content={title} />
	<meta name="twitter:description" content={description} />
	{#if image}<meta name="twitter:image" content={image} />{/if}
	{#if jsonld}
		{#each (Array.isArray(jsonld) ? jsonld : [jsonld]) as block}
			{@html `<script type="application/ld+json">${JSON.stringify(block).replace(/</g, '\\u003c')}</script>`}
		{/each}
	{/if}
</svelte:head>
```
`path` is passed in as an already-ABSOLUTE URL by every caller (built from `PUBLIC_SITE_URL` server-side — see below), not a relative path, since `og:url`/canonical must be absolute per spec. `.replace(/</g, '\\u003c')` on the JSON-LD payload is a deliberate, minimal XSS guard: it's `{@html}`-injected raw (Svelte doesn't let you put a `<script type="application/ld+json">` tag through normal templating and have the browser treat it as data, since `<svelte:head>` script tags are otherwise treated as executable by SvelteKit's own head-injection unless marked `application/ld+json` — using `{@html}` with escaped `<` is the standard safe pattern for this exact case, since `JSON.stringify` output could otherwise contain a literal `</script` sequence breaking out of the tag if a title/description ever contained one).

**3. Wire a sane fallback into `app.html`.** `src/app.html` (already read) currently has no title/description at all as a fallback for the rare page that doesn't render `SeoHead` (error pages, the offline fallback). Add directly before `%sveltekit.head%`:
```html
		<title>x2 — find your people, one room at a time</title>
		<meta name="description" content="search rooms built around what you're into, join in a click, or match one-to-one. no feed, no profile to perform for." />
```
Any page that renders `<SeoHead>` overrides these via `<svelte:head>`'s well-defined override-by-later-tag behavior (SvelteKit deduplicates `<title>` by taking the last one encountered in the render tree) — this is purely the floor for pages that render neither.

**4. Wire it into the home page**, since it's the highest-traffic page and already has final copy from [[rewrite_site_copy]]/[[rebuild_home_as_room_search]] (both already executed by the time this plan runs — this repo's `plan/site_reorientation.plan.json` is a separate, prerequisite plan). In `src/routes/+page.svelte`, add at the top:
```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	import SeoHead from '$lib/components/SeoHead.svelte';
	import { env } from '$env/dynamic/private'; // WRONG — env is server-only, not available in a .svelte file
</script>
```
Correction — `$env/dynamic/private` cannot be imported into a `.svelte` file (client-reachable code); the absolute URL must be assembled server-side and passed down as page data. In `src/routes/+page.server.ts` (already built by [[rebuild_home_as_room_search]]), add `site_url: env.PUBLIC_SITE_URL` to the returned object, then in `+page.svelte`:
```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	import SeoHead from '$lib/components/SeoHead.svelte';
	let { data } = $props();
</script>

<SeoHead
	title="find your people, one room at a time"
	description="search rooms built around what you're into, join in a click, or match one-to-one. no feed, no profile to perform for."
	path={data.site_url}
/>
```
This step only wires the home page as the reference implementation — [[add_meta_titles_to_every_route]] does the exhaustive per-route pass (every other route, correct `noindex` per route, dynamic titles for room/user pages).

