add_json_ld_structured_data.s:
Structured data is the single highest-leverage technical SEO change for AI-answer-engine visibility (ChatGPT/Perplexity/Gemini/Claude web search all weight machine-readable entity data heavily when deciding what to cite for a query like "omegle alternative") — this step adds the two site-wide blocks plus a reusable breadcrumb builder; per-page types (BlogPosting, FAQPage) are added alongside the routes that need them in [[add_blog_routes]].

**1. Organization + WebSite + SearchAction, on the home page.** `WebSite` with a `SearchAction` is what enables Google's sitelinks searchbox and signals to any crawler (human-search or AI-search) that this site has an internal search worth using directly. Extend the home page's `<SeoHead>` call from [[add_public_site_url_and_seo_head_component]] with a `jsonld` prop:
```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	import SeoHead from '$lib/components/SeoHead.svelte';
	let { data } = $props();
	const jsonld = [
		{
			'@context': 'https://schema.org',
			'@type': 'Organization',
			name: 'x2',
			url: data.site_url,
			logo: `${data.site_url}/logo.svg`
		},
		{
			'@context': 'https://schema.org',
			'@type': 'WebSite',
			name: 'x2',
			url: data.site_url,
			potentialAction: {
				'@type': 'SearchAction',
				target: `${data.site_url}/?q={search_term_string}`,
				'query-input': 'required name=search_term_string'
			}
		}
	];
</script>

<SeoHead
	title="find your people, one room at a time"
	description="search rooms built around what you're into, join in a click, or match one-to-one. no feed, no profile to perform for."
	path={data.site_url}
	{jsonld}
/>
```
`target` uses `/?q=` because [[rebuild_home_as_room_search]] already wired the home page's search form to submit `?q=` as a GET, per that step's own markup (`<form method="GET">`, `name="q"` input) — confirm this still matches exactly before finalizing; if that step's param name differs, use the actual one.

**2. Breadcrumb helper.** Most of this app's public/indexable surface is two levels deep at most (home → room, home → blog post), but breadcrumbs are cheap, real ranking/CTR signal (they render as the URL path in Google's result snippet instead of a raw URL), and directly help an AI answer engine understand page hierarchy when deciding what to cite. Add to `src/lib/seo.ts` (new file, shared client+server-safe pure functions — no `$env` import, so this file is safe to import from `.svelte` files directly unlike server-only modules):
```ts
export function breadcrumb_jsonld(items: { name: string; url: string }[]): Record<string, unknown> {
	return {
		'@context': 'https://schema.org',
		'@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
		itemListElement: items.map((item, i) => ({
			'@type': 'ListItem',
			position: i + 1,
			name: item.name,
			item: item.url
		}))
	};
}
```
Used by [[add_blog_routes]] (home → blog → post) and [[add_alternative_landing_pages]] (home → alternatives → omegle).

