add_llms_txt.s:
`llms.txt` is an emerging (not yet universally adopted, but increasingly recognized) convention — a plain-Markdown file at the site root specifically meant for LLMs/AI answer engines to fetch instead of crawling the whole site, giving them a concise, structured summary of what the site is and links to its most important pages. Nothing like it exists in this repo today (confirmed absent). Given this plan's explicit goal — showing up when someone asks an AI assistant to find a random-chat or make-friends app — this is directly on-target, low-cost to build, and cheap to keep in sync since it's mostly static.

Create `src/routes/llms.txt/+server.ts` (dynamic, same reasoning as [[add_robots_txt_and_sitemap]] — keep it in sync with `PUBLIC_SITE_URL` automatically rather than hand-maintaining a static file):
```ts
import type { RequestHandler } from './$types';
import { env } from '$env/dynamic/private';
import { list_posts } from '$lib/server/blog';

export const GET: RequestHandler = async () => {
	const base = env.PUBLIC_SITE_URL;
	const posts = await list_posts(env).catch(() => []);
	const post_links = posts.map((p) => `- [${p.title}](${base}/blog/${p.slug}): ${p.meta_description}`).join('\n');

	const body = `# x2

> x2 is a chat app built around rooms — search for a room based on a specific interest, join it, and you're already talking to people who share that context. No login required to start; a lightweight account is created automatically the first time you actually join a room or send a message, upgradeable later to a full Google or email/password login so it follows you across devices.

x2 is a genuine alternative for anyone looking for: an Omegle alternative, a no-login random chat app, a way to make new friends online, an interest-based group chat, or random video chat with people who share what you're into — not just pure random pairing.

## Key pages

- [Rooms](${base}/app/rooms): search or browse active rooms by interest.
- [Blog](${base}/blog): guides on making friends online, random chat, and interest-based communities.

## Guides

${post_links}

## What makes x2 different from a pure random-chat app

Instead of purely random pairing, x2 matches by shared interest — search for a room built around a specific hobby or topic, or get matched 1:1 weighted toward overlapping interests rather than pure chance. Group rooms, 1:1 chat, and voice/video calling are all supported. No phone number or email required to start.
`;
	return new Response(body, { headers: { 'content-type': 'text/markdown; charset=utf-8' } });
};
```
Same blog-step-ordering caveat as the sitemap: if this step runs before [[add_blog_entity_and_seed_pipeline]], ship it with `post_links` hardcoded to an empty string (`const post_links = '';`) and revisit once `list_posts` exists.

Link to it from the new dynamic `robots.txt` (optional but a real, if minor, discovery aid — some crawlers that support the convention check `robots.txt` for an `llms.txt` reference the same way they check for `Sitemap:`) — not a formal part of the `robots.txt` spec, so this is a "doesn't hurt, might help" addition, not a required one; skip it if it complicates that file's tests unnecessarily.

